{{- /*
The "enum" template is the entry point invoked by the generator's
pipeline. It composes the partial templates that together form one
enum _test.go file:

  - "header"     — package + import block + file-level doc
  - "enum-type"  — Test<Type>Enum function per requested type, with
                   subtests covering exhaustiveness, distinctness,
                   zero-value, wire compatibility, and the
                   method-gated subtests (stringer, parse, marshal
                   text/json/binary)

Each partial is independently regression-tested in templates_test.go
so changes to one don't silently break the others.
*/ -}}
{{define "enum"}}
{{template "header" .}}
{{- range $e := .Enums}}
{{template "enum-type" (dict "Type" $e "Local" $)}}
{{- end}}
{{end}}
